From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:44:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 427/488] [DS4.1] The fused decode router reads the padding
 mask and input ids

Every forward negated the step's padding mask for the routers and, in a
vision model, compared the input ids with the image sentinels: torch
kernels in the target's and the drafter's graphs. route_partials now
takes the padding mask as it is (a set row is skipped; a CED decoder's
routing mask keeps its sense) and compares the ids itself. The TileKernels
path for longer batches keeps the shared masks.
---
